\f0\fs36 \cf0 Program Structure\
\
Because there's really no Tektronix 405X IDE available, you'll want to do program design and organization in some kind of external document. You can party like it's 1979 by using a legal pad (or some kind of engineering notebook) and a pencil, or maybe a text file on a computer.  Keeping track of what the program is about, and what sections of line numbers belong to whatever logical components that you're using.\
\
Traditionally programs start at line 100. This is s nice round line number that skips over all of the User-Definable key definitions from lines 4 through 84. You have three lines of code at the very start that you can use for a GOTO 100, maybe set up an interrupt handler or two first-thing.\
\

\f1\i Some ideas - using the tape append to load common routines.\
